`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Which frequencies each axis gets",children:[e.jsx(i.p,{children:"In Week 3's RoPE the frequency falls from pair to pair: low-numbered pairs rotate fast, high-numbered pairs slowly. Which pairs MRoPE gives to each axis therefore decides which frequencies that axis gets."}),e.jsxs(i.p,{children:[e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Chunked MRoPE."})," Qwen2-VL gives each axis one contiguous block of pairs ",e.jsx(t,{id:"bai2025qwen3vl",children:"Bai et al., 2025b"}),', so each axis gets one band of frequencies. On our reading of the released Qwen2-VL-7B configuration and code, its 64 pairs split 16, 24 and 24. Time takes pairs 0 to 15, the fastest. Height takes pairs 16 to 39, and width pairs 40 to 63, the slowest. The Qwen3-VL report judges the result: "This results in an imbalanced frequency spectrum, which subsequent studies have shown to degrade performance on long-video understanding benchmarks" ',e.jsx(t,{id:"bai2025qwen3vl",children:"Bai et al., 2025b"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(i.p,{children:[e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Interleaved MRoPE."}),' Qwen3-VL instead redesigns "the frequency allocation by interleaving the t, h, and w components across the embedding dimensions". According to the report, this "ensures that each spatial–temporal axis is uniformly represented across both low- and high-frequency bands", and the caption of its Figure 1 speaks of "a balanced frequency spectrum" ',e.jsx(t,{id:"bai2025qwen3vl",children:"Bai et al., 2025b"}),". In the released code (our reading), the first 60 pairs go to time, height and width in turn, and the last 4 pairs, the slowest, go to time alone. That gives the 24/20/20 split, so the alternation is not perfectly even: height and width miss the four slowest frequencies."]}),e.jsx(i.p,{children:"Bonus 2's reading of RoPE suggests why this matters, an inference the report does not make: fast pairs tell nearby positions apart, and slow pairs tell distant ones apart. The report's own reason for the change is its sentence on long-video benchmarks."})]})]}),e.jsxs(n,{title:"Video time is written as text",accent:4,number:"13",items:"4",children:[e.jsxs(i.ul,{children:[`
